# Shapes qj evaluates without a full parse (PassthroughPath in src/filter/mod.rs:
# identity, length/keys/type/has on a field chain, map(.f), map({f, g}),
# map(builtin), with or without a prefix) crossed with adversarial documents:
# duplicate keys, escapes, number spellings, non-object elements, NaN,
# 1e1000. The file mode is the one that reaches the passthroughs.
#
# Format: jq's .test format (see tests/jq_compat/jq.test), without expected
# output lines: each case is a program line followed by one input line, and
# cases are separated by blank lines. jq_diff runs every case under jq 1.8.1
# and qj in compact, pretty, file and ndjson modes and compares stdout, exit
# code and stderr byte for byte; jq's output is the expectation.

